    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** leading the charge, posting a commanding 86.04 efficiency score. Facing Ure\u00f1a, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite .474 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against a pitcher with a 4.55 xERA, making him the clear anchor of the offense. We are also leaning heavily into top-of-the-order production today: **Trea Turner** (74.03) and **Christian Yelich** (72.61) provide excellent returns, bolstered by strong lineup positioning and double-digit boosts from platoon advantages. While **Kyle Schwarber** (70.71) faces a similarly strong setup against Phillips, the real value lies in the volume of opportunities provided to these leadoff and second-spot hitters, which serves as a force multiplier for our Roto category targets.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Chase Meidroth**, who sits at a 51.59 efficiency score. While **Chase Meidroth** offered a solid floor, he was ultimately bypassed due to a challenging matchup against Fried and a lower projected ceiling compared to our starting middle infielders like **Colt Keith**, whose score of 64.42 is fueled by a significant +7% platoon boost and a prime #3 spot in the order. Elsewhere, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** carries a slight warning; while his 58.94 score is solid, he faces a 15% penalty due to his dynamic platoon split against Liberatore, making him a player we will monitor closely for mid-game defensive substitution should his at-bats prove unproductive. We remain disciplined regarding our game caps, leaving **Josh Smith** and **Lars Nootbaar** on the bench to preserve our flexibility for more favorable platoon alignments later in the week, while **Junior Caminero** remains sidelined by a team off-day.",
